{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"9d48ab4f1540c1d9d943ac17f5378c0f3a5e6ebe44ade593f4fe36200400bde9","digest":{"component_or_area":"Bridge git delivery / push retry","key_entities":["src/rebar/_store/push.py","src/rebar/_store/push_classify.py","_is_non_fast_forward","_is_policy_decline","_recover_non_fast_forward","_merge_remote_under_lock","server certificate verification failed","could not fetch from promisor remote","push-transport-failed","push-policy-declined","merge-recovery-blocked","_MAX_RETRIES","_GIT_TIMEOUT"],"problem_keywords":["git delivery","transport failure","TLS certificate verification","retry logic","push failure","transient fault","backoff","converged reconcile"],"propositions":["Bridge git delivery abandons after a single transport failure (TLS handshake, DNS, timeout) instead of retrying, leaving converged work unpushed and lost","Transport faults and policy violations are currently treated identically as terminal, but transport errors are transient and retriable while policy violations are permanent","The push retry logic has no backoff mechanism; existing non-fast-forward retries fire back-to-back without delay","Promisor remote fetch failures during merge recovery (blob:none partial clone) are not classified as transport-retriable and block recovery","A policy decline must remain strictly terminal (one attempt, no retries) while transport faults should retry up to 3 times with exponential backoff (0.5s, 2.0s)"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787495182785871001,"uuid":"eba16a66-1457-47d7-beef-3a8653a51773"}